hadiths[578]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes care of an orphan, whether his own or someone else's, he and I will be (together) in Paradise like these two (fingers)."""
"4449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone was whiter than snow until the sins of the children of Adam turned it black."""
"4450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man (among the people) before you would be seized, a pit would be dug for him in the ground and he would be made to stand in it. Then a saw would be brought and placed on his head, and he would be split into two pieces, yet that would not turn him away from his religion. And his flesh would be combed away from his bones and sinews with iron combs, yet that too would not turn him away from his religion. By Allah! Allah will surely complete this religion, until a rider travels from San'a to Hadramawt fearing no one but Allah, and (fearing) the wolf for his sheep. But you are being hasty."""
"4451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first to show hospitality to guests was Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."""
"4452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of the Jahiliyyah used to say: Bad omens are only in a woman, an animal and a house."""
"4453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dawud (peace be upon him) was the most devoted in worship of all human beings."""
"4454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man used to lend to people, and he would say to his servant: When you come to someone in hardship, forgive him; perhaps Allah will forgive us. So he met Allah, and Allah forgave him."""
"4455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There were two men among the Children of Israel who were like brothers to each other. One of them was a sinner and the other was diligent in worship. The worshipper would constantly see the other in sin and say: Stop it. One day he found him in sin again and said: Stop it. He said: Leave me to my Lord; have you been sent as a watcher over me?! So he (the worshipper) said: By Allah! Allah will never forgive you, or Allah will never admit you into Paradise. Then the souls of both of them were taken, and they both gathered before the Lord of the worlds. Allah Almighty said to this worshipper: Did you have knowledge of Me, or did you have power over what is in My hand?! And He said to the sinner: Go and enter Paradise by My mercy. And He said about the other: Take him to Hell."""
"4456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakariyya (peace be upon him) was a carpenter."""
"4457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ashura was a day on which the people of the Jahiliyyah used to fast. So whoever among you wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever wishes to leave it, let him leave it."""
"4458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There was a branch of a tree on the road that used to harm people. A man removed it from the road, and he was admitted into Paradise."""
"4459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There was a man among the Children of Israel who had killed ninety-nine people. Then he went out asking (about the way to repentance), and he came to a monk and asked him. He said: Is there repentance for me? The monk said: No. So he killed him as well. Then he kept on asking, and a man said to him: Go to such-and-such a town. Death overtook him on the way, and he inclined his chest towards that town. Then the angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed about him. Allah Almighty revealed to this (town): Draw near, and revealed to that (town): Move away, and said: Measure the distance between the two places. They found him closer to this one (the town he was heading for) by a hand-span, so he was forgiven."""
"4460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You used to have two days on which you would play, and Allah has given you in exchange for them two days better than them: the day of Eid al-Fitr and the day of Eid al-Adha."""
"4461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the people before you there was a king who had a sorcerer. When he grew old, he said to the king: I have grown old, so send me a boy so that I may teach him sorcery. So the king sent him a boy for him to teach. On the boy's way there lived a monk; he would sit with him and listen to his words, and he came to like them. So whenever he went to the sorcerer, he would pass by the monk and sit with him, and when he reached the sorcerer, the sorcerer would beat him. He complained about this to the monk, and the monk said: When you go to the sorcerer, say: My family held me back; and when you go to your family, say: The sorcerer held me back. While he was in this state, a huge beast suddenly came and blocked the people's way. He said: Today I will know whether the sorcerer is better or the monk. He picked up a stone and said: O Allah, if the monk's way is more beloved to You than the sorcerer's way, then kill this beast so that the people may pass. He threw the stone, the beast died, and the people passed. He came to the monk and told him, and the monk said: My son, today you are better than me. Your affair has reached the level that I see, and you will surely be tested, so do not tell anyone where I am. The boy would cure the one born blind and the leper, and heal people of other diseases as well. A companion of the king who had become blind heard of this, and he came to him with many gifts and said: All this is yours if you cure me. The boy said: I do not cure anyone; only Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, cures. If you believe in Allah, I will pray to Allah and He will cure you. So he believed in Allah, and Allah cured him. Then he came to the king and sat with him as he used to sit before. The king asked him: Who restored your sight? He said: My Lord. The king said: Do you have a lord other than me? He said: My Lord and your Lord is Allah. So the king seized him and kept torturing him until he pointed out the boy. The boy was brought, and the king said to him: My son, your sorcery has reached the point that you cure the one born blind and the leper, and you do this and that! The boy said: I do not cure anyone; only Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, cures. So the king seized him and kept torturing him until he pointed out the monk. The monk was brought and told: Turn back from your religion. He refused, so a saw was sent for, placed in the middle of his head, and he was sawn through until his two halves fell apart. Then the king's companion was brought and told: Turn back from your religion. He too refused, so the saw was placed in the middle of his head and he was sawn through until his two halves fell apart. Then the boy was brought and told: Turn back from your religion. He refused, so the king handed him over to some of his men and said: Take him to such-and-such a mountain and make him climb it; when you reach its summit, if he turns back from his religion (well and good), otherwise throw him down. So they took him and made him climb the mountain, and the boy said: O Allah, save me from them in whatever way You will. The mountain shook, they all fell, and the boy came walking to the king. The king asked: What happened to your companions? He said: Allah saved me from them. The king then handed him over to some other men of his and said: Take him, put him on a boat and take him to the middle of the sea; if he turns back from his religion (well and good), otherwise throw him into the sea. So they took him, and the boy said: O Allah, save me from them in whatever way You will. The boat capsized with them and they all drowned, and the boy came walking to the king. The king asked: What happened to your companions? He said: Allah saved me from them. Then the boy said to the king: You cannot kill me until you do what I command you. The king asked: What is it? The boy said: Gather the people on one open plain and crucify me on a tree trunk, then take an arrow from my quiver, place it in the middle of the bow, then say: In the name of Allah, the Lord of this boy, and then shoot. If you do that, you will be able to kill me. So the king gathered the people on one open plain and crucified him on a tree trunk, then took an arrow from his quiver, placed it in the middle of the bow and said: In the name of Allah, the Lord of this boy, and then shot the arrow, and it struck him in the temple. He placed his hand on the spot where the arrow had struck and died. The people said: We believe in the Lord of this boy, we believe in the Lord of this boy, we believe in the Lord of this boy. The king was approached and told: Have you seen what you used to fear? By Allah, the very thing you feared has befallen you; the people have believed! So the king had trenches dug at the entrances of the roads, had fires lit in them and said: Whoever does not turn back from his religion, throw him into it. And so it was done, until a woman came carrying her child, and she hesitated to fall into it. Her child said to her: Mother, be patient, for you are on the truth."""
"4462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of the prophets used to draw lines (on the ground), so whoever's (lines) agree with his line, then that is fine."""
"4463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This matter (of rule) was among (the people of) Himyar, then Allah took it away from them and placed it in Quraysh, and it will soon return to them (Himyar)."""
"4464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A short woman of the Children of Israel used to walk with two tall women, so she had two legs made of wood, and took a gold ring, covered it with clay, then filled it with musk, which is the best of perfumes. One day she passed between the two women and they did not recognise her, and she gestured with her hand like this."""
"4465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There were two women who had their sons with them. A wolf came and took away the son of one of them. Her companion said: It has taken your son; and the other said: No, it has taken your son. They both went to Dawud (peace be upon him) for judgement, and he judged in favour of the older woman. Then they both left and went to Sulayman bin Dawud (peace be upon him) and told him what had happened. Sulayman (peace be upon him) said: Bring me a knife, and I will cut him in two between them. The younger woman said: Do not do it, may Allah have mercy on you; he is her son. So Sulayman (peace be upon him) judged in favour of the younger woman."""
"4466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel were governed by the prophets; whenever a prophet died, another prophet succeeded him. And there is no prophet after me, but there will soon be caliphs, and they will be many. The Companions asked: Then what do you command us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Fulfil the pledge of allegiance to the first, then to the one after him, and give them their due right that Allah has appointed for them, for Allah will surely ask them about the responsibility that was entrusted to them."""
"4467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel used to bathe naked together, looking at one another, while Musa (peace be upon him) used to bathe alone. They said: By Allah, nothing prevents Musa from bathing with us except that he suffers from a scrotal swelling. One day Musa (peace be upon him) went to bathe and placed his garment on a stone, and the stone ran off with his garment. Musa (peace be upon him) ran after it, saying: My garment, O stone! My garment, O stone! Until the Children of Israel saw Musa (peace be upon him) and said: By Allah, there is nothing wrong with Musa. Then he took his garment and began striking the stone."""
"4468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is as if I am looking at Musa (peace be upon him) in this valley, in the state of ihram, wrapped in two (particular kinds of) cloaks."""
"4469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is as if I am looking at him: a black man with widely spaced legs, demolishing it (the Ka'bah) stone by stone."""
"4470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is as if I am looking at Yunus (peace be upon him), riding a she-camel whose halter is made of palm fibre, wearing a woollen cloak and saying: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk (Here I am, O Allah, here I am)."""
"4471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give precedence to the elder, give precedence to the elder."""
"4472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Book of Allah (prescribes) retaliation (qisas)."""
"4473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Book of Allah is the rope of Allah that is stretched from the heaven to the earth."""
"4474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty wrote down the decrees of all creatures fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and at that time His Throne was upon the water."""
"4475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your Lord wrote upon Himself with His hand, before He created the creation: My mercy has prevailed over My wrath."""
"4476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam's share of zina (fornication) has been written for him, and he will inevitably attain it. The zina of the eyes is looking, the zina of the ears is listening, the zina of the tongue is speaking, the zina of the hand is seizing, the zina of the foot is walking, and the heart desires and wishes, and the private part confirms it or denies it."""
"4477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kikh, kikh (spit it out)! Throw it away. Do you not know that we do not eat charity (sadaqah)?"""
"4478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking it when he is alive."""
"4479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sin enough that you withhold (maintenance) from the one whose sustenance is in your control."""
"4480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sin enough for a man that he narrates everything he hears."""
"4481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sin enough for a man that he neglects the one whose sustenance is his responsibility."""
"4482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is enough of a lie for a man that he narrates everything he hears."""
"4483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The flashing of swords over a person's head is enough of a (great) trial for him."""
"4484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a snake, a single strike of your whip is enough for you, whether you hit it or miss it."""
"4485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Disowning one's lineage, however insignificant it may be, is disbelief in Allah."""
"4486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is disbelief on a man's part that he claims a lineage that is not known, or denies his own lineage, however insignificant it may be."""
"4487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The expiation for a gathering is that the servant says: 'Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta wahdaka la sharika laka, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk' (Glory be to You, O Allah, and all praise is Yours. I bear witness that there is no true god but You alone, You have no partner. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance)."""
"4488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If nothing (specific) is named in a vow, its expiation is (the same as) the expiation for an oath."""
"4489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The expiations for sins are: performing ablution completely despite difficulties (cold or discomfort), walking on foot to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after a prayer."""
"4490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your evil away from people, for that is a charity from you upon your own self."""
"4491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your belching away from us, for the one who was most full in this world will be hungry the longest on the Day of Resurrection."""
"4492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your children in (from going out) at the time of Isha, for at that time the jinn spread out and snatch."""
"4493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat garlic. Were it not that I converse privately with the angel, I too would have eaten it."""
"4494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat. By my life, whoever has eaten in return for a false ruqyah (incantation), you have eaten (in contrast to him) in return for a true ruqyah."""
"4495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat whatever your bow (its arrow) brings back to you."""
"4496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat whatever cuts the veins, unless it was gnawed with a tooth or torn with a nail."""
"4497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat from the wealth of your orphan, without extravagance or wastefulness, and do not accumulate his wealth (for yourself), and do not protect your own wealth by means of his wealth."""
"4498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat olive oil and anoint (your body) with it, for it is from a blessed tree."""
"4499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat from the edges of the vessel, saying Bismillah, and leave its top part, for blessing descends upon it from above."""
"4500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat together and do not eat separately, for blessing is in togetherness."""
"4501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat together and do not eat separately, for the food of one person suffices for two, and the food of two suffices for three and four. Eat together and do not eat separately, for blessing is in togetherness."""
"4502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat from the edges of the bowl and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle."""
"4503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat the meat of the sacrificial animals and store it as well."""
"4504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat from its edges and leave its peak (the top part); blessing will be placed in it."""
"4505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat, drink, give charity and wear clothes, without extravagance and without arrogance."""
"4506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat and drink, and do not let the rising whiteness (of dawn) deceive you; so keep eating and drinking until the redness appears (spreading) before you."""
"4507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat it, and whoever of you eats it should not come near this mosque until its smell has gone (that is, after eating garlic)."""
"4508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The earth devours the entire body of the son of Adam except the tailbone (the last part of the spine); from it he was created and from it he will be reassembled."""
"4509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The wealth, honour and blood of every Muslim are sacred (forbidden) to every other Muslim, and it is enough evil for a man that he looks down upon his Muslim brother."""
"4510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every man will be in the shade of his charity until judgement is passed between the people."""
"4511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every man, that deed is made easy for which he was created."""
"4512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All of my Ummah will be pardoned except those who sin openly. And part of sinning openly is that a man does a deed (a sin) at night, then wakes up in the morning while Allah Almighty has concealed it for him, and he says: I did such and such last night. He spent the night with his Lord concealing him, and as soon as morning comes he himself removes the cover that Allah had placed over him."""
"4513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All of my Ummah will enter Paradise except the one who refuses. Whoever obeys me will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has indeed refused."""
"4514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every one of the people of Paradise will see his place in Hell that could have been his, and he will say: Had Allah not guided me, this would have been my end. So this will be a cause of gratitude for him. And every one of the people of Hell will see his place in Paradise that could have been his, and he will say: If only Allah had guided me. So this will be a cause of regret for him."""
"4515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every one of the children of Adam is a sinner, and the best of sinners are those who repent often."""
"4516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever any of the children of Adam is born, Satan jabs him in his side with his finger, except Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him). Satan wanted to jab him too, but his jab struck the veil."""
"4517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every one of the children of Adam is touched by Satan on the day his mother gives birth to him, except Maryam (peace be upon her) and her son."""
"4518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Both the seller and the buyer have the option to cancel the sale as long as they have not separated, except for a sale in which an option (condition) was agreed beforehand."""
"4519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every body that has been nourished on unlawful (earnings), the Fire is more fitting for it."""
"4520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every sermon in which there is no tashahhud (testimony of faith) is like a mutilated hand."""
"4521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every step that any of you takes towards the prayer, a good deed is recorded for him and a sin is erased from him."""
"4522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything that Allah Almighty has created is beautiful."""
"4523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every supplication remains held back (from the heavens) until blessings are sent upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every sin is such that it is hoped Allah will forgive it, except for the one who dies as a polytheist or kills a believer deliberately."""
"4525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eating any predatory animal with fangs is unlawful."""
"4526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every shepherd (guardian) is answerable for those under his care."""
"4527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection every tie and lineage will be severed except my tie and my lineage."""
"4528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity is due upon every joint of a person on every day on which the sun rises. Judging justly between two people is charity; helping a man with his mount, by seating him upon it or lifting his belongings onto it, is also charity; a good word is charity; every step taken towards the prayer is charity; showing the way is charity; and removing something harmful from the path is charity."""
"4529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."""
"4530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it be a hundred conditions."""
"4531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything is according to divine decree, even incapacity and cleverness."""
"4532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever part of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire."""
"4533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever is cut from a living (animal) is (in the ruling of) carrion."""
"4534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything that is not part of the remembrance of Allah is idle amusement and play, except four things: a man playing with his wife, a man training his horse, a man walking between two targets (to practise archery), and a man learning to swim."""
"4535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prayer in which Surah al-Fatihah is not recited is deficient."""
"4536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole plain of Arafah is a place of standing, all the land of Mina is a place of sacrifice, the whole plain of Muzdalifah is a place of standing, and all the streets of Makkah are a way and a place of sacrifice."""
"4537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole plain of Arafat is a place of standing, but stay above the valley of Uranah; the whole plain of Muzdalifah is a place of standing, but stay above the valley of Muhassir; all the streets of Mina are a place of sacrifice; and all the days of Tashriq are days of slaughter."""
"4538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed of the son of Adam is multiplied from ten times up to seven hundred times, and even more, as much as Allah wills, except fasting. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Fasting is for Me and I Myself will reward it; he (the fasting person) leaves his desire and his food for My sake. For the fasting person there are two joys: one when he breaks his fast and the other when he meets his Lord. And the smell of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasing to Allah than the fragrance of musk."""
"4539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After a man dies, every deed of his is cut off, except the one who guards the frontier in the path of Allah; his deeds keep increasing for him until the Day of Resurrection and he continues to receive provision."""
"4540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every eye commits adultery, and when a woman applies perfume and passes by a gathering, she is an adulteress."""
"4541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every child is held in pledge for his aqiqah; (an animal) should be slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, his head should be shaved and he should be given a name."""
"4542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every loan given is charity."""
"4543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every division that was made in the time of ignorance (Jahiliyyah) shall remain as it was divided, and every division that Islam has reached shall be according to the division of Islam."""
"4544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every wound that a Muslim receives in the path of Allah will be on the Day of Resurrection in the same state as when it was inflicted, blood will be flowing from it; its colour will be the colour of blood, but its fragrance will be like musk."""
"4545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything that (intoxicates a person and) makes him heedless of prayer is forbidden."""
"4546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever you do for your family is charity (sadaqah) upon them."""
"4547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All the wealth of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is charity, except what he fed his family and clothed them with. Indeed, we (the Prophets) do not leave inheritance."""
"4548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicant is wine (khamr) and every intoxicant is forbidden. Whoever drinks an intoxicant, his prayer for forty days becomes deficient. Then if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance, and if he repeats (the same sin) a fourth time, it becomes a right upon Allah that He make him drink from Tinat al-Khabal, that is, the pus of the people of Hell. And whoever gives an intoxicant to drink to a child who does not recognise what is lawful for him from what is unlawful, it also becomes a right upon Allah that He make him drink from Tinat al-Khabal."""
"4549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every person whose lineage was attributed, after the death of his (claimed) father, to that father by his heirs: if he is from a slave woman whom the (father) owned on the day he had relations with her, then he is joined to the one who attributed him (to himself), but he has no share in the inheritance that was divided before this; as for the inheritance that has not yet been divided, he will get his share of it. And if that father, to whom his lineage is being claimed, had himself denied him, then he will not be joined. And if he is from a slave woman whom the (father) did not own, or from a free woman with whom he committed fornication, then he will neither be joined to him nor will he inherit. And even if the one to whom his lineage is being claimed had himself claimed him, he is still a child of fornication and (his lineage) is with his mother's people, whoever they are, whether she is free or a slave woman."""
"4550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicant is forbidden."""
"4551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicant is forbidden, and whoever drinks an intoxicant, it is a covenant upon Allah that He will make him drink from Tinat al-Khabal, that is, the sweat (pus) of the people of Hell."""
"4552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicant is forbidden, and of whatever a measure (faraq) intoxicates, even a handful of it is forbidden."""
"4553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicant is wine (khamr) and every intoxicant is forbidden. Whoever drinks wine in this world and dies while addicted to it without repenting, he will not drink it in the Hereafter."""
"4554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every image-maker is in the Fire. For every image he made, a soul will be created that will punish him in Hell."""
"4555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."""
"4556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity, and the one who guides to good is like the one who does it."""
"4557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity, and among good deeds is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face, and that you pour water from your bucket into your neighbour's vessel."""
"4558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed you do for a rich person or a poor person is charity."""
"4559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every child is born upon the fitrah (the natural disposition of Islam) until his tongue speaks clearly for him; then his parents make him a Jew, a Christian or a Magian."""
"4560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every child is born upon the (true) religion; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian, and make him a polytheist."" It was said: ""Then what about the one who dies before that?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah knows best what they would have done."""
"4561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For everyone, that deed has been made easy for which he was created."""
"4562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deeds of every person who dies are sealed, except the one who dies guarding the frontier in the path of Allah; his deeds continue to grow until the Day of Resurrection, and he is kept safe from the trial of the grave."""
"4563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every woman who wails (over the dead) lies, except Umm Sa'd."""
"4564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection every tie of lineage and of marriage will be cut off, except my lineage and my ties of marriage."""
"4565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every person among the children of Adam is a master: the man is the master of his family, and the woman is the mistress of her house."""
"4566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever a servant (of Allah) spends, he is rewarded for it, except (what is spent on) buildings."""
"4567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every oath that is sworn by other than Allah is shirk (associating partners with Allah)."""
"4568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All of you are the children of Adam (peace be upon him), and Adam was created from dust. People who boast about their forefathers must certainly desist, or else they will become more contemptible in the sight of Allah than dung beetles."""
"4569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you is a guardian, and each of you will be asked about those in his charge. The ruler is a guardian and he will be asked about those in his charge; a man is the guardian of his family and he will be asked about those in his charge; a woman is the guardian of her husband's house and she will be asked about those in her charge; a servant is the guardian of his master's wealth and he will be asked about what is in his charge; and a man is the guardian of his father's wealth and he will be asked about what is in his charge. So each of you is a guardian, and each of you will be asked about those in his charge."""
"4570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All of you will enter Paradise, except the one who runs away from Allah as a camel runs away from its owners."""
"4571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The words of relief from distress are: 'La ilaha illallahul-Halimul-Karim, la ilaha illallahul-Aliyyul-Azim, la ilaha illallahu Rabbus-samawatis-sab'i wa Rabbul-Arshil-Karim' (There is no true god except Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no true god except Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent; there is no true god except Allah, the Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Noble Throne)."""
"4572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two phrases are light on the tongue, heavy in the Scale, and beloved to the Most Merciful: 'Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi', 'Subhanallahil-Azim' (Glory be to Allah and with His praise; glory be to Allah, the Magnificent)."""
"4573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many a person with dishevelled hair, covered in dust and wearing worn-out clothes, is paid no attention, yet if he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfil it. Among them is al-Bara' bin Malik."""
"4574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many hanging date clusters there are in Paradise for Ibn al-Dahdah!"""
"4575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just as grapes are not picked from thorns, likewise the wicked will not attain the stations of the righteous. So take whichever path you wish; whichever path you take, you will arrive at its people."""
"4576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just as grapes are not picked from thorns, likewise the wicked will not attain the stations of the righteous. These are only two paths; whichever of them you take, you will reach your destination accordingly."""
"4577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just as the reward is multiplied for us, so too is the trial multiplied upon us."""
"4578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Many among men attained perfection, but none among women attained perfection except Asiyah, the wife of Pharaoh, and Maryam bint Imran. And the superiority of Aishah over other women is like the superiority of tharid over all other food."""
"4579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be in this world as if you were a stranger or a traveller."""
"4580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be scrupulously pious, and you will be the most devout worshipper among people; be content, and you will be the most grateful among people; love for people what you love for yourself, and you will be a believer; treat your neighbour well, and you will be a Muslim; and laugh little, for much laughter deadens the heart."""
"4581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was a Prophet even when Adam (peace be upon him) was still between the soul and the body (in the stage of creation)."""
"4582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you (from keeping nabidh in vessels) other than leather vessels; now you may drink from every vessel, only take care that you do not drink an intoxicant."""
"4583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from (certain) vessels; now you may make nabidh in them, but avoid every intoxicant."""
"4584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves. Listen! Now visit them, for it softens the heart, brings tears to the eye and reminds of the Hereafter; but do not say anything indecent (during the visit)."""
"4585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from (keeping) the meat of the sacrificial animals beyond three days, so that those with means would be generous towards those who have none. Now eat as much as you wish, feed others and store it."""
"4586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remain at these sacred sites (masha'ir) of yours, for today you are upon one of the legacies of the legacy of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."""
"4587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stand in the row that is closest to me."""
"4588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when rulers are imposed over you who delay the prayer from its time? Pray the prayer at its time; then if you find them praying it, pray with them as well, and it will be a voluntary (nafl) prayer for you."""
"4589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when you are unable to collect (from the protected non-Muslims) either a dinar or a dirham? The covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger will be violated, so Allah will harden the hearts of the protected people (ahl al-dhimmah), and they will withhold what is in their hands."""
"4590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when Isa, the son of Maryam (peace be upon him), descends among you and he leads you in prayer?"""
"4591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when Isa, the son of Maryam (peace be upon him), descends among you while your imam is from among yourselves?"""
"4592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when the one with the Horn (the angel) has put the Horn to his mouth, bowed his forehead and inclined his ear, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow so that he blows?"" The Companions said: ""What should we say?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: Allah is sufficient for us and He is the best Disposer of affairs; in Allah we have put our trust."""
"4593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be when rulers come over you who pray the prayer outside its proper time? Pray the prayer at its proper time, and make the prayer you pray with them (again) a voluntary prayer."""
"4594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you be in a time that is soon to come, in which people will be sifted out as though through a sieve and only the dregs of people will remain, whose covenants and trusts will have become confused; they will fall into disagreement and become like this - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers -? At that time, hold to what you recognise and leave what you consider (false), turn to your own particular affairs and leave the affairs of the general public."""
"4595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What would you say about the joy of a man whose mount broke loose from him and ran off dragging its halter in a barren land where there is neither food nor water, carrying his food and water upon it; he searched for it and could not find it until it became very hard for him; then it passed by the stump of a tree and its halter got caught on it, and he found it caught there? Listen! By Allah, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than that man at (finding) his mount."""
"4596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How then (can I do it), when (about me) it has already been said?"""
"4597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will Allah purify a nation in which the weak cannot take his right from the strong without any hindrance?"""
"4598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will Allah purify a nation in which the right of the weak is not taken from the strong?"""
"4599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Measure your food (grain and the like), for blessing lies in food that is measured."""
"4600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Measure your food, and you will be blessed in it."""
"4601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and swearing a false oath."""
"4602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are: associating partners with Allah, slandering a chaste woman, killing a believing soul, fleeing from the battlefield of jihad, consuming the wealth of an orphan, disobedience to Muslim parents, and deviating in (violating) the sanctity of the House (the Ka'bah), which is your qiblah both in life and in death."""
"4603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are: associating partners with Allah, despairing of the relief of Allah, and losing hope in the mercy of Allah."""
"4604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, and disobedience to parents. Shall I not tell you of the greatest of the major sins? It is (speaking) false words."""
"4605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are nine, the greatest of them being associating partners with Allah; then killing a soul unjustly, consuming usury (riba), consuming the wealth of an orphan, slandering a chaste woman, fleeing from the battlefield of jihad, disobedience to parents, and treating as lawful (the violation of) the sanctity of the Ka'bah, which is your qiblah both in life and in death."""
"4606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The major sins are seven: associating partners with Allah, unjustly killing the soul that Allah has made sacred, slandering a chaste woman, fleeing from the battlefield of jihad, consuming usury (riba), consuming the wealth of an orphan, and returning to Bedouin life after the emigration (Hijrah)."""
"4607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give precedence to the elder, give precedence to the elder."""
"4608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Arrogance is to reject the truth and to look down on people."""
"4609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Applying kohl (antimony) an odd number (of times) is (Sunnah)."""
"4610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble: Yusuf bin Ya'qub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim (peace be upon them)."""
"4611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The pure black dog is a devil."""
"4612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Truffles (al-kam'ah) are from the manna that Allah Almighty sent down upon the Children of Israel, and their water is a cure for the eye."""
"4613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Truffles are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."""
"4614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise which Allah has given me. Its soil is musk; it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Birds come down to it whose necks are like the necks of camels, and the one who eats them will be in greater delight than they are."""
"4615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise. Its two banks are of gold, it flows over pearls and rubies, its soil is more fragrant than musk, and its water is sweeter than honey and whiter than snow."""
"4616","""The last words of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were: Attend to the prayer, attend to the prayer, and fear Allah regarding the slaves (male and female) whom your right hands possess."""
"4617","""The last thing he (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke was that he said: May Allah destroy the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as places of prostration. Beware! Two religions shall not remain in the land of the Arabs."""
"4618","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The most hateful thing among creation to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was lying."""
"4619","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was white, as though he had been cast from silver, and his (peace and blessings be upon him) hair was straight."""
"4620","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was white tinged with redness, his blessed head was large — his eyelashes were thick."""
"4621","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) whiteness was tinged with redness, the pupils of his eyes were black and his eyelashes were thick."""
"4622","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was white, handsome and of medium height."""
"4623","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The colour most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was green."""
"4624","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The garment most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was the hibarah (a striped Yemeni cloak)."""
"4625","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The garment most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was the qamis (long shirt)."""
"4626","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The religious (deed) most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was that which the one doing it persisted in."""
"4627","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The drink most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was a sweet and cold drink."""
"4628","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""What he (peace and blessings be upon him) loved most was to fast in the month of Sha'ban, and then to join it with Ramadan."""
"4629","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The meat on the bone most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was the foreleg of a goat."""
"4630","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The deed most beloved to him (peace and blessings be upon him) was that which is done consistently, even if it is little."""
"4631","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When relieving himself, he (peace and blessings be upon him) most preferred to screen himself behind a mound or a cluster of date palms."""
"4632","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was the best of all people in character."""
"4633","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was the best of all people in appearance and the most handsome. He (peace and blessings be upon him) was of medium height, inclining to tall; the distance between his (peace and blessings be upon him) two shoulders was quite broad; his (peace and blessings be upon him) cheeks were smooth; his hair was deep black; his eyes looked as though lined with kohl; his eyelashes were thick; when he put his foot down, he put it down with the whole foot; the sole of his (peace and blessings be upon him) foot had no hollow. When he (peace and blessings be upon him) removed his cloak from his shoulders, it was as though he were an ingot of silver."""
"4634","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most handsome of people, the most generous of people and the bravest of people."""
"4635","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most handsome of people in face and the best of them in character; he (peace and blessings be upon him) was neither conspicuously tall nor short."""
"4636","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When leading others, he (peace and blessings be upon him) was the lightest of people in the prayer he led for the people, and the longest of people in the prayer he prayed for himself."""
"4637","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Despite performing the prayer completely, he (peace and blessings be upon him) was the lightest of all people in prayer."""
"4638","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the door of a people, instead of standing directly facing the door, he would stand at its right or left side and say: As-salamu alaykum, as-salamu alaykum."""
"4639","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) visited a sick person, or a sick person was brought to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would make this supplication: O Lord of mankind! Remove the affliction and grant cure, You are the One who cures; there is no cure except Your cure, a cure that leaves no illness behind."""
"4640","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When something pleasing came to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would say: 'Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi bi-ni'matihi tatimmus-salihat' (All praise is for Allah, by whose favour good deeds are completed), and when something displeasing came to him, he would say: 'Al-hamdu lillahi 'ala kulli hal' (All praise is for Allah in every circumstance)."""
"4641","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a man came to him (peace and blessings be upon him) with a name that he (peace and blessings be upon him) did not like, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would change it."""
"4642","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the fay' (spoils taken without fighting) came to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would distribute it the same day, giving the married man two shares and the unmarried man one share."""
"4643","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a people brought their charity (sadaqah) to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'O Allah, send Your mercy upon the family of so-and-so.'"""
"4644","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the first fruit of the season was brought to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would place it on his eyes, then on his lips, then he would give it to whichever children were with him (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4645","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When food was brought to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would ask whether it was a gift or charity. If it was said that it was charity, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say to his Companions: 'You eat,' and he himself would not eat. And if it was said that it was a gift, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would stretch out his hand and eat with them."""
"4646","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When his (peace and blessings be upon him) family were afflicted with fever, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would order hasa' (a broth-like food) to be made; then, when it was made, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would order them to drink it, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'It soothes the grieving heart and removes sorrow from the heart of the sick, just as one of you women removes dirt from her face with water.'"""
"4647","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down on his bed, he would place his right hand under his right cheek."""
"4648","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down on his bed, he would recite the surah 'Say: O disbelievers' (Qul ya ayyuhal-kafirun) until he completed it."""
"4649","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down on his bed at night, he would say: 'In the name of Allah I have laid down my side. O Allah, forgive me my sin, drive away my devil, release my pledge (my soul), make my scale heavy, and place me in the Highest Assembly.'"""
"4650","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down on his bed at night, he would place his hand under his cheek, then say: 'Bismika Allahumma ahya wa bismika amut' (O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die). And when he woke up, he would say: 'Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi ahyana ba'da ma amatana wa ilayhin-nushur' (All praise is for Allah who gave us life after He had caused us to die, and to Him is the rising)."""
"4651","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to relieve himself, he would go far away."""
"4652","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to relieve himself, he would not lift his garment until he was close to the ground."""
"4653","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to be intimate with one of his wives while she was menstruating, he would instruct her to wrap a waist-cloth (izar) around herself, and then he would be intimate with her."""
"4654","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to enter the state of ihram, he would apply the best perfume he could find."""
"4655","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to supplicate against someone or for someone, he would perform qunut after the bowing (ruku')."""
"4656","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to sleep, he would place his right hand under his cheek, then say three times: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.'"""
"4657","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to bid farewell to an army, he would say: 'I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts and the final outcomes of your deeds.'"""
"4658","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to perform i'tikaf, he would pray the Fajr prayer, then enter his place of i'tikaf."""
"4659","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah), he would perform ablution (wudu) like the ablution for prayer; and when he intended to eat or drink while in a state of janabah, he would wash his hands, then eat and drink."""
"4660","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah), he would wash his private parts and perform ablution (wudu) like the ablution for prayer."""
"4661","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to travel, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them had her lot drawn, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would take her with him."""
"4662","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended a military expedition, he would, in order to mislead the enemy, give the impression of some other direction instead of it."""
"4663","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) intended some intimacy with a menstruating (wife), he would place a cloth over her private part."""
"4664","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) wore a new garment, he would call it by its name, whether it was a shirt, a turban or a cloak, then say: 'O Allah, to You belongs all praise; You have clothed me with it. I ask You for its good and the good of that for which it was made, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of that for which it was made.'"""
"4665","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When news was slow in coming to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would recite this verse of Tarafah (the poet): 'The one you did not provision (to bring news) will bring you the news.'"""
"4666","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for rain, he would say: 'O Allah, give water to Your servants and Your animals, spread Your mercy, and give life to Your dead land.'"""
"4667","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) began the prayer, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and all praise is Yours; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You.'"""
"4668","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) used the tooth-stick (siwak), he would give the siwak to the eldest, and when he drank, he would give (the remainder) to the one on his right."""
"4669","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the cold was severe, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray the prayer early, and when the heat was severe, he would delay the prayer (until it was cooler)."""
"4670","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a strong wind blew, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would supplicate: 'O Allah, make it fertile (bringing rain), not barren.'"""
"4671","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When someone complained of pain in his head, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'Go and have cupping done.' And when someone complained of pain in his foot, he would say: 'Go and apply henna to it.'"""
"4672","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill, Jibril (peace be upon him) would perform ruqyah over him (peace and blessings be upon him) and say: 'In the name of Allah; He cures you of every illness, and (He protects you) from the evil of an envier when he envies and from the evil of everyone with an (evil) eye.'"""
"4673","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill, he would recite the Mu'awwidhat, blow over himself, and pass his hand over his body."""
"4674","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the morning and when he reached the evening, he would say: 'We have reached the morning upon the natural way (fitrah) of Islam, upon the word of sincerity, upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and upon the creed of our father Ibrahim (peace be upon him), who was upright, a Muslim, and was not of the polytheists.'"""
"4675","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) came to know that someone from his household had told a lie, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would keep turning away from him until he repented."""
"4676","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) tied a turban, he would let its end hang down between his two shoulders."""
"4677","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) broke his fast with a people, he would say: 'Those fasting have broken their fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have descended upon you.'"""
"4678","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) broke his fast, he would say: 'The thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, if Allah wills.'"""
"4679","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) broke his fast with a people, he would say: 'Those fasting have broken their fast with you, and the angels have sent blessings upon you.'"""
"4680","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) applied kohl, he would apply it an odd number of times, and when he cleaned himself with stones (istijmar), he would do so an odd number of times."""
"4681","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) ate or drank something, he would say: 'Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi at'ama wa saqa wa sawwaghahu wa ja'ala lahu makhraja' (All praise is for Allah who gave food and drink, made it easy to swallow, and made for it a way out)."""
"4682","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) ate food, he would lick his three fingers."""
"4683","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) ate, his (peace and blessings be upon him) fingers would not go beyond (the food) in front of him."""
"4684","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the two circumcised parts met, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"4685","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When revelation was sent down upon him (peace and blessings be upon him), a heaviness would come over him (peace and blessings be upon him) and his (peace and blessings be upon him) face would change colour."""
"4686","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When revelation was sent down upon him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would lower his head, and his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions would also lower their heads; then, when the revelation ceased, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would raise his head."""
"4687","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer, he would turn away from the qiblah to the right or the left."""
"4688","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) finished his prayer, he would seek forgiveness three times, then say: 'O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honour.'"""
"4689","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: 'Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi at'amana wa saqana wa kafana wa awana, fakam mimman la kafiya lahu wa la mu'wiya lah' (All praise is for Allah who fed us, gave us drink, sufficed us and gave us shelter; for how many are there who have no one to suffice them and no one to give them shelter)."""
"4690","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When people gave him (peace and blessings be upon him) the pledge of allegiance, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would teach them these words: 'As far as I am able.'"""
"4691","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) sent one of his Companions for some task, he would say: 'Give glad tidings and do not drive people away, and make things easy and do not make them difficult.'"""
"4692","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When something reached him (peace and blessings be upon him) about a man, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not say: 'What is the matter with so-and-so that he says such a thing?' Rather, he would say: 'What is the matter with people who say such and such?'"""
"4693","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) turned over in his sleep at night, he would say: 'La ilaha illallahu al-Wahidu al-Qahhar, Rabbu as-samawati wal-ardi wa ma baynahuma al-Azizu al-Ghaffar' (There is no true god but Allah, the One, the Subduer of all, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the Almighty, the Oft-Forgiving)."""
"4694","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) said something, he would repeat it three times so that it would be understood, and when he (peace and blessings be upon him) came to a people and greeted them with salam, he would greet them three times."""
"4695","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed Tahajjud, he would give the salam after every two rak'ahs."""
"4696","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he would take a handful of water, bring it under his chin and run it through his beard, and he would say: My Lord has commanded me to do so."""
"4697","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he would take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his private parts."""
"4698","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he would pass the water around both his elbows (making sure it reached them well)."""
"4699","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he would run water through his beard."""
"4700","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, he would rub between the toes of his feet with his little finger."""
"4701","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When news that pleased him came to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would fall down in prostration in gratitude to Allah Almighty."""
"4702","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) sat, he would sit in ihtiba' with his hands (clasping his knees)."""
"4703","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a matter troubled him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray."""
"4704","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) swore an oath, he would not break it, until the ruling on the expiation for oaths was revealed."""
"4705","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) swore an oath, he would say: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4706","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) feared a people, he would say: O Allah, we place You before them (as a shield), and we seek refuge in You from their evil."""
"4707","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) came out of the toilet, he would say: O Allah, I ask for Your forgiveness."""
"4708","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) left his house, he would say: In the name of Allah, I have put my trust in Allah. O Allah, we seek refuge in You from slipping or going astray, from doing wrong or being wronged, and from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly."""
"4709","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) left his house, he would say: In the name of Allah. O Lord, I seek refuge in You from slipping or going astray, from doing wrong or being wronged, and from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly."""
"4710","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went out on the day of Eid by one route, he would return by another."""
"4711","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon, his (peace and blessings be upon him) eyes would turn red, his voice would rise and his anger would intensify, as though he (peace and blessings be upon him) were someone warning of an army's attack, saying: The enemy is about to attack you in the morning or the evening."""
"4712","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the toilet, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female evil jinn."""
"4713","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the last ten days of Ramadan began, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would tighten his waist-wrapper, spend his nights awake (in worship), and wake his family as well."""
"4714","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the toilet, he would say: In the name of Allah. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female evil jinn."""
"4715","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque, he would say: I seek refuge in Allah the Magnificent, in His Noble Face and in His eternal authority from Satan the accursed. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever says this is protected from him (Satan) for the rest of the day."""
"4716","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque, he would say: O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and upon the wives of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4717","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered his house, the first thing he did was use the miswak."""
"4718","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went to visit a sick person, he would say: No harm; if Allah wills, this illness is a purification (washing away sins)."""
"4719","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) entered a house, he would say: Do you have any food? If he was told no, he would say: Then I am fasting."""
"4720","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated, he would begin with himself."""
"4721","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated, he would turn the inner side of his palms towards his face."""
"4722","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) slaughtered a sheep, he would say: Send some of it to the friends of Khadijah."""
"4723","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned someone and supplicated for him, he would first supplicate for himself."""
"4724","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went to relieve himself, he would go far away."""
"4725","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) saw rain, he would say: O Allah, make it a beneficial rain."""
"4726","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) saw the new crescent moon, he would say: O Allah, let it rise over us with blessing and faith, with safety and Islam. O moon, my Lord and your Lord is Allah."""
"4727","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) saw something he liked, he would say: 'Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi bi-ni'matihi tatimmus-salihat' (All praise is for Allah, by whose favour good deeds are completed), and when he saw something he disliked, he would say: 'Alhamdu lillahi 'ala kulli hal' (All praise is for Allah in every circumstance)."""
"4728","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When something alarmed him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would say: Allah, Allah is my Lord; He has no partner."""
"4729","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) congratulated someone who had married, he would say: May Allah bless you, send blessings upon you, and keep the two of you together in goodness."""
"4730","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head from bowing in the last rak'ah of the Fajr prayer, he would recite the qunut."""
"4731","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When his (peace and blessings be upon him) dining cloth was lifted, he would say: 'Alhamdu lillahi hamdan kathiran tayyiban mubarakan fih, alhamdu lillahil-ladhi kafana wa awana, ghayra makfiyyin wa la makfurin wa la muwadda'in wa la mustaghnan 'anhu, Rabbana' (Abundant, pure and blessed praise is for Allah; all praise is for Allah who has sufficed us and given us shelter; praise that is never enough, never denied, never abandoned, and never to be dispensed with, O our Lord)."""
"4732","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed, he would keep his back so level that if water were poured on it, it would stay in place."""
"4733","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed, he would spread his fingers apart, and when he prostrated, he would keep his fingers together."""
"4734","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed, he would say three times: Subhana Rabbiyal-'Azimi wa bi-hamdih (Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent, and praise be to Him), and when he prostrated, he would say three times: Subhana Rabbiyal-A'la wa bi-hamdih (Glory be to my Lord the Most High, and praise be to Him)."""
"4735","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went to stone the Jamarat, he would walk on foot, going and returning."""
"4736","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, he would move on and not stop there."""
"4737","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) asked Allah for something, he would turn the inner side of both his palms towards Him."""
"4738","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) prostrated, he would hold his arms so far away from his sides that the whiteness of his (peace and blessings be upon him) armpits could be seen."""
"4739","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) was pleased, his (peace and blessings be upon him) face would shine as though it were a piece of the moon."""
"4740","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer with the salam, he would sit only as long as it takes to say: O Allah, You are Peace and from You comes peace; Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honour."""
"4741","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) heard the mu'adhdhin, he would say the same as he said, until, when he said 'Hayya 'alas-salah, hayya 'alal-falah' (Come to prayer, come to success), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no ability to avoid sin and no strength to do good except by the enabling of Allah)."""
"4742","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) heard the mu'adhdhin pronouncing the testimony of faith, he would say: And I too, I too bear witness."""
"4743","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) heard an unpleasant name, he would change it to one better than it."""
"4744","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) drank something, he would breathe three times and say: This is more pleasant, more wholesome and more healthful."""
"4745","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit, he would greet with salam."""
"4746","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed the Fajr prayer, the people of Madinah would come to him (peace and blessings be upon him) with their vessels containing water, and whatever vessel was brought, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would dip his hand into it."""
"4747","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed the Fajr prayer, he would remain sitting in his place of prayer until the sun rose."""
"4748","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed the Fajr prayer on a journey, he would walk a little away from his mount."""
"4749","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed the two sunnah rak'ahs of Fajr, he would lie down on his right side."""
"4750","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed a prayer, he would keep to it consistently."""
"4751","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed tawaf around the Ka'bah, he would touch the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner in every circuit."""
"4752","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) halted to rest during the night, he would lie down with his head on his right hand, and when he halted shortly before dawn, he would place his head on the palm of his right hand and keep his forearm upright."""
"4753","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a strong wind blew, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: O Allah, I ask You for its good, the good of what is in it and the good of that with which it has been sent, and I seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of what is in it and the evil of that with which it has been sent."""
"4754","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) sneezed, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would praise Allah, and it would be said to him (peace and blessings be upon him): May Allah have mercy on you. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."""
"4755","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) sneezed, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would place his hand or his garment over his mouth and lower his voice."""
"4756","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) did a deed, he would keep to it consistently."""
"4757","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went out on a military expedition, he would say: O Allah, You alone are my support and You alone are my helper; by Your help alone I move, by Your strength alone I attack, and for Your sake alone I fight."""
"4758","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) became angry, both his (peace and blessings be upon him) cheeks would turn red."""
"4759","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) missed the four rak'ahs before Zuhr, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray them after Zuhr."""
"4760","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) had finished burying the deceased, he would stand at his grave and say: Seek forgiveness from Allah for your brother and ask for steadfastness for him, for he is being questioned right now."""
"4761","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood for prayer, he would raise both his hands fully extended."""
"4762","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood on the pulpit, his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions would turn their faces towards him (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4763","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) got up at night to pray, he would begin his prayer with two light rak'ahs."""
"4764","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) got up from sleep at night, he would clean his mouth with the tooth-stick (miswak)."""
"4765","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from a journey, the children of his (peace and blessings be upon him) household would come out to receive him (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"4766","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', he would say: 'Subhana Rabbiya al-A'la' (Glory be to my Lord, the Most High)."""
"4767","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) recited in prayer at night, he would sometimes raise his voice and sometimes lower it."""
"4768","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When food was placed before him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: Bismillah (In the name of Allah). And when he had finished, he would say: O Allah, You have fed, given drink, enriched, provided sufficiency in the means of life, guided and chosen. O Allah, to You alone belongs all praise for what You have given."""
"4769","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from a military expedition, Hajj or Umrah, he would say the takbir three times on every elevated place of the land, then he would say: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd, wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. Ayibuna, ta'ibuna, 'abiduna, sajiduna, li-Rabbina hamidun. Sadaqallahu wa'dah, wa nasara 'abdah, wa hazamal-ahzaba wahdah' (There is no true god but Allah, He is alone and has no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. We are returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, and praising our Lord. Allah has fulfilled His promise, helped His servant, and alone defeated the confederate armies of the enemy)."""
"4770","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When fresh dates were available, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would break his fast only with fresh dates, and when fresh dates were not available, he would break his fast with dried dates."""
"4771","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) was in bowing (ruku') or prostration, he would say: O Allah, You are free of all imperfection and Yours alone is the praise; I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance."""
"4772","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) was fasting, he would order a man to climb onto some high place, and when that man said that the sun had set, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would break his fast."""
"4773","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) was in an odd-numbered rak'ah of his prayer, he would not stand up until he had sat up fully."""
"4774","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When it was the day before the Day of Tarwiyah, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would address the people in a sermon and inform them of their rites (of Hajj)."""
"4775","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) was resident, he would observe i'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan, and when he was on a journey, he would observe i'tikaf for twenty days the following year."""
"4776","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When it was the day of Eid, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would take a different route (on his return)."""
"4777","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When some matter distressed him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: O Ever-Living, O Sustainer of all! In Your mercy I seek relief."""
"4778","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked something, it would become apparent on his (peace and blessings be upon him) face."""
"4779","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) put on a shirt, he would begin with the right side."""
"4780","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When one of his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions met him (peace and blessings be upon him) and stood with him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not turn away until that man himself left. And when one of his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions met him (peace and blessings be upon him) and took hold of his (peace and blessings be upon him) hand, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not withdraw his hand until that man himself withdrew his hand. And when he (peace and blessings be upon him) met one of his Companions and that Companion drew close to his (peace and blessings be upon him) ear and took hold of it, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not pull it away until that man himself moved away."""
"4781","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When one of his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions met him (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) would touch him affectionately and supplicate for him."""
"4782","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When, during recitation, he (peace and blessings be upon him) passed a verse that spoke of the fear of punishment, he would seek refuge; when he passed a verse of mercy, he would ask Allah (for it); and when he passed a verse that declared Allah's transcendence, he would glorify Him."""
"4783","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When any member of his (peace and blessings be upon him) household fell ill, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite the Mu'awwidhat and blow over him."""
"4784","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) walked, he would lift his feet firmly."""
"4785","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) walked, it was as if he (peace and blessings be upon him) were leaning on something."""
"4786","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) walked, he would not look back."""
"4787","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) walked, his (peace and blessings be upon him) Companions would walk in front of him (peace and blessings be upon him) and leave his (peace and blessings be upon him) back for the angels."""
"4788","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) slept through the night (missing his night prayer) or fell ill, he would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day."""
"4789","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) slept, he would breathe with a light sound."""
"4790","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) went to sleep, he would place his right hand under his cheek and make this supplication: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."""
"4791","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When some worry or grief befell him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would make this supplication: O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining! Through Your mercy I call for help."""
"4792","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When revelation came down upon him (peace and blessings be upon him), a heaviness would come over him because of it, and sweat like pearls would pour from his forehead, even if it was the cold season."""
"4793","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) stopped at a halting place, he would not move on without praying the Zuhr prayer."""
"4794","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) had intercourse with one of his wives and felt reluctant to get up (for the ritual bath), he would strike his hand on the wall and perform tayammum."""
"4795","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) bade farewell to a man, he would take hold of his hand and would not let go of it until the man himself withdrew his hand, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'Astawdi'ullaha dinaka wa amanataka wa khawatima 'amalik' (I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust and the final outcome of your deeds)."""
"4796","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) placed the deceased in his grave, he would say: 'Bismillahi wa billahi wa fi sabilillahi wa 'ala millati Rasulillah' (In the name of Allah, with the help of Allah, in the path of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah)."""
"4797","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most merciful of all people towards children and family."""
"4798","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) complexion was radiant (white tinged with red), his sweat glistened like pearls, and when he walked he would lean forward."""
"4799","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was more modest than a secluded virgin girl."""
"4800","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The oath he (peace and blessings be upon him) swore most often was: 'No, by the One who turns the hearts (Allah)!'"""
"4801","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) most frequent supplication was: 'Ya Muqallib al-qulub, thabbit qalbi 'ala dinik' (O Turner of the hearts, keep my heart firm upon Your religion). He was asked about this, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'There is no human being except that his heart is between two of the fingers of Allah; whomever He wills He keeps firm, and whomever He wills He causes to deviate.'"""
"4802","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The supplication he (peace and blessings be upon him) made most often was: 'Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"""
"4803","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Most of his (peace and blessings be upon him) fasts were on Saturday and Sunday, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'These two are the festival days of the polytheists, so I love to oppose them.'"""
"4804","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) fasted most often on Monday and Thursday. He was asked about this, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday, and every Muslim is forgiven except two people who have cut off relations with each other, and Allah Almighty says: Give these two respite.'"""
"4805","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""People would knock at his (peace and blessings be upon him) door with their fingernails."""
"4806","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) eyes would sleep, but his heart would not sleep."""
"4807","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The Seal of Prophethood was on his (peace and blessings be upon him) back in the form of a raised piece of flesh."""
"4808","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) Seal of Prophethood was like a red gland, the size of a pigeon's egg."""
"4809","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) ring was of silver, and its stone was also of silver."""
"4810","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) ring was of silver, and its stone was Abyssinian (a stone from Abyssinia)."""
"4811","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) character was the Qur'an."""
"4812","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) banner was black and his standard was white."""
"4813","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was of medium height, neither excessively tall nor short; his complexion was radiant (white tinged with red), neither pale white nor brown; and his hair was neither tightly curled nor completely straight."""
"4814","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was merciful towards his family."""
"4815","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) was merciful, and whoever came to him, he would make him a promise, and if he had something with him, he would fulfil it for him."""
"4816","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had long forearms, broad shoulders and thick eyelashes."""
"4817","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) hair was shorter than a jummah (hair reaching the shoulders) and longer than a wafrah (hair reaching the earlobes)."""
"4818","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) white hairs numbered about twenty."""
"4819","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) head, both hands and both feet were large."""
"4820","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) head was large and his beard was thick."""
"4821","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a wide mouth, reddish eyes and heels with little flesh."""
"4822","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would remain silent for long periods and laughed little."""
"4823","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There was deliberateness and gentleness in his (peace and blessings be upon him) speech."""
"4824","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perspire a great deal."""
"4825","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The hair of his (peace and blessings be upon him) beard was thick."""
"4826","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) speech was clear and distinct, understood by everyone who heard it."""
"4827","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) sandal had two straps."""
"4828","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a large bowl which had four rings attached to it."""
"4829","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a donkey whose name was Ufayr."""
"4830","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a towel with which he would dry himself after ablution."""
"4831","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a small container of perfume from which he would apply fragrance."""
"4832","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a wooden vessel which was kept under his bed, and he would urinate in it at night."""
"4833","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a large bowl called 'al-Gharra', which four men would carry."""
"4834","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had two callers to prayer (mu'adhdhins): Bilal and the blind Companion Ibn Umm Maktum."""
"4835","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) had a sheet dyed with wars and saffron, which he would wear when going round to his wives in turn, and when it was the night of one of the wives, she would sprinkle that sheet with water."""
"4836","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Among the things he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say to the servant was: 'Do you need anything?'"""
"4837","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""His (peace and blessings be upon him) face was radiant like the sun and the moon, and it was round."""
"4838","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The pillow on which he (peace and blessings be upon him) slept at night was of leather, stuffed with palm fibre."""
"4839","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The call to prayer (adhan) was not given for the two Eid prayers."""
"4840","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not eat while reclining, nor would two men walk behind him treading on his heels."""
"4841","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) did not take bad omens, but rather took good omens."""
"4842","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever he (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up during the night, he would always pass the tooth-stick (miswak) over his mouth."""
"4843","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not perform a fresh ablution after the ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"4844","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Often He (peace and blessings be upon him) could not find even enough poor-quality dates to fill his stomach."""
"4845","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr without eating something, and on the day of Eid al-Adha he would not eat anything until he had offered the sacrifice."""
"4846","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not store anything away for the next day."""
"4847","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) never left out four rak'ahs before Zuhr and two rak'ahs before Fajr."""
"4848","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) did not leave the fasts of the White Days (the 13th, 14th and 15th of every month), neither when travelling nor when at home."""
"4849","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) never left the night prayer (qiyam al-layl), and when he was ill or felt lethargic, he would pray sitting."""
"4850","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The people who came near him (peace and blessings be upon him) were neither pushed away nor beaten."""
"4851","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not go back (on a matter) after three days."""
"4852","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) never refused perfume."""
"4853","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever He (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up from sleep at night, he would always use the tooth-stick (miswak)."""
"4854","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever anything was asked of him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would either give it or remain silent."""
"4855","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would touch (istilam) only the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner."""
"4856","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) did not shake hands with women at the time of the pledge of allegiance (bay'ah)."""
"4857","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not pray the two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah and the two rak'ahs after Maghrib anywhere other than in his own house."""
"4858","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not pray Maghrib without first breaking his fast, even if only with a sip of water."""
"4859","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not pray any prayer before Eid, but when he returned to his house he would pray two rak'ahs."""
"4860","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever He (peace and blessings be upon him) suffered a wound or was pricked by a thorn, he would apply henna to it."""
"4861","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would only smile; he did not laugh out loud."""
"4862","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not come upon his family unexpectedly at night."""
"4863","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) did not make the sermon long on the day of Jumu'ah."""
"4864","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not know that a surah had ended until 'Bismillahir-Rahmanir-Rahim' (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) was revealed to him."""
"4865","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not set out early on the morning of Eid al-Fitr without eating some dates."""
"4866","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not complete the Qur'an in less than three days."""
"4867","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever He (peace and blessings be upon him) rose from a gathering, he would always say: 'Subhanakallahumma Rabbi wa bihamdika, la ilaha illa anta, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk' (Glory be to You, O Allah, my Lord, and with Your praise; there is no true god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance). And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever says these words when rising from his gathering will be forgiven the slips he committed in that gathering."""
"4868","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever anything was asked of him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would almost always fulfil it."""
"4869","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would almost never say 'no' to anything. When something was asked of him and he wished to do it, he would say: Yes; and if he did not wish to do it, he would remain silent."""
"4870","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When He (peace and blessings be upon him) walked, he would not turn to look behind him."""
"4871","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whatever was asked of him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would not refuse to give it."""
"4872","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever He (peace and blessings be upon him) slept, the tooth-stick (miswak) would be beside his head, and when he woke up, the first thing he did was use the tooth-stick."""
"4873","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not sleep without reciting Surah al-Sajdah (Alif Lam Mim, Tanzil) and Surah al-Mulk (Tabarakalladhi biyadihil-mulk)."""
"4874","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would not sleep without reciting Surah Bani Isra'il and Surah al-Zumar."""
"4875","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When dates containing worms were brought to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would inspect them and take the worms out of them."""
"4876","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When children were brought to him (peace and blessings be upon him), he would pray for blessing upon them, perform tahnik for them (chewing a date and placing it in the child's mouth), and supplicate for them."""
"4877","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go to the weak Muslims, visit them, visit their sick and attend their funerals."""
"4878","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat watermelon with fresh dates."""
"4879","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat watermelon with fresh dates and say: I break the heat of this with the coolness of this, and the coolness of this with the heat of this."""
"4880","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat cucumber with fresh dates."""
"4881","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would accept a gift and eat from it, but he would not eat from charity (sadaqah)."""
"4882","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat with three fingers and lick his hand before wiping it clean."""
"4883","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat food cooked on fire, then pray without performing a fresh ablution."""
"4884","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command us to have ruqyah performed for protection against the evil eye."""
"4885","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command that the zakah be given before going out to the prayer on the day of Eid al-Fitr."""
"4886","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command the freeing of slaves on the occasion of the eclipse prayer."""
"4887","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command the dyeing of white hair, in opposition to the non-Arabs."""
"4888","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command his daughters and his wives to go out to the Eid prayer ground on the two Eids."""
"4889","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command whoever accepted Islam to be circumcised."""
"4890","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would command that when any one of them intended to sleep, she should say Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, Subhan Allah thirty-three times and Allahu Akbar thirty-three times."""
"4891","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would be intimate with his wives while they were menstruating, over the lower garment (izar)."""
"4892","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When He (peace and blessings be upon him) broke his fast, he would begin with dates."""
"4893","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go out to the green low-lying valleys."""
"4894","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would send to the places of ablution, and water would be brought from there, and he would drink it, hoping for the blessing of the hands of the Muslims."""
"4895","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would spend several consecutive nights hungry, and his family would find no evening meal, and their bread was mostly barley bread."""
"4896","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sell the produce of the date-palm orchards of Banu al-Nadir and keep back for his family their provision for a year."""
"4897","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would take particular care to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."""
"4898","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wear a silver ring."""
"4899","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wear a ring on his left hand."""
"4900","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wear a ring on his right hand."""
"4901","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""On journeys, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would stay behind the caravan, urge the weak forward, let them ride with him, and supplicate for them."""
"4902","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to seek refuge from the jinn and from the evil eye of man, until the Mu'awwidhatan (Surah al-Falaq and Surah al-Nas) were revealed. When they were revealed, he adopted them and left everything besides them."""
"4903","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would seek refuge from severe trial, from being overtaken by misery, from an evil decree, and from the gloating of enemies."""
"4904","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would take good omens and would not take bad omens, and he liked a good name."""
"4905","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite this verse of poetry as an illustration: And news will be brought to you by one whom you did not provision (to bring it)."""
"4906","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform ablution, then kiss his wife and pray, without performing ablution again."""
"4907","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform ablution at the time of every prayer."""
"4908","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."""
"4909","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sometimes perform ablution washing each part once, sometimes twice, and sometimes three times; he adopted all of these ways."""
"4910","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""In the last ten days of Ramadan, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would strive as he did not strive on any other days."""
"4911","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would keep the stone of his ring towards his palm."""
"4912","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would use his right hand for eating, drinking, ablution, putting on clothes, taking and giving, and his left hand for other tasks."""
"4913","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit, he would sit until the mu'adhdhin finished the call to prayer. Then he would stand and deliver the sermon, then sit and not speak, then stand and deliver the sermon again."""
"4914","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sit on his buttocks with his knees drawn up."""
"4915","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sit on the ground, eat sitting on the ground, hold the goat himself (for milking), and even accept the invitation of a slave to eat barley bread."""
"4916","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would eat melon and fresh dates together."""
"4917","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""While travelling, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would combine the Zuhr and Asr prayers, and the Maghrib and Isha prayers."""
"4918","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to begin with the right side as much as possible in his purification, putting on his shoes, combing his hair, and in all his affairs."""
"4919","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked sweets and honey."""
"4920","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked gourd."""
"4921","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked butter and dates."""
"4922","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked dry date-palm stalks, and one of them was always in his hand."""
"4923","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) set out for jihad, he liked to set out on a Thursday."""
"4924","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and the Ansar to stand close to him in prayer, so that they could remember the prayer from him."""
"4925","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would have himself cupped."""
"4926","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would have himself cupped on his head and between his shoulders, and he would say: Whoever lets out blood by cupping in this way, it will not harm him even without any other medicine."""
"4927","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would have himself cupped on the two veins of the neck and between the shoulders, and he would have himself cupped on the 17th, 19th and 21st of the month."""
"4928","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would have himself cupped on his head and would call it 'Umm Mughith'."""
"4929","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would speak so deliberately, pausing between his words, that if someone wished to count them, he could count them."""
"4930","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would swear this oath: No, by the Turner of hearts (Allah)!"""
"4931","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would carry Zamzam water with him."""
"4932","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go to the Eid prayer ground on foot and return on foot."""
"4933","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go to the two Eids on foot, pray without the adhan or the iqamah, and then return on foot by another route."""
"4934","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go out on the two Eids raising his voice with the tahlil and takbir."""
"4935","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would deliver the sermon every Friday with Surah Qaf."""
"4936","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would deliver the sermon standing, sit between the two sermons, recite verses, and admonish the people."""
"4937","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sew his own clothes, mend his own shoes, and do the work that men do in their homes."""
"4938","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Dawn would sometimes come upon he (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) because of his wife; then he would take a ritual bath (ghusl) and fast."""
"4939","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would be invited even to barley bread and stale fat."""
"4940","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""At times of distress, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would supplicate: 'La ilaha illallahul-'Azimul-Halim, la ilaha illallahu Rabbul-'Arshil-'Azim, la ilaha illallahu Rabbus-samawatis-sab'i wa Rabbul-ardi wa Rabbul-'Arshil-Karim' (There is no true deity except Allah, the Mighty, the Forbearing; there is no true deity except Allah, the Lord of the Mighty Throne; there is no true deity except Allah, the Lord of the seven heavens, the Lord of the earth, and the Lord of the Noble Throne)."""
"4941","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would visit all his wives in turn within a single hour of the night and day."""
"4942","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would slaughter his sacrificial animal with his own hand."""
"4943","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to remember Allah Almighty at all of his times."""
"4944","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would let his lower garment hang down in front and keep it raised at the back."""
"4945","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would let someone ride behind him, place his food on the ground, accept the invitation of a slave, and ride a donkey."""
"4946","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would ride a donkey, mend his sandals himself, keep the hem of his shirt raised, wear woollen clothing, and say: 'Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me.'"""
"4947","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would visit the Ansar, greet their children with salam, and pass his hand over their heads."""
"4948","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would burn pure aloeswood as incense, and he would mix camphor with it."""
"4949","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked comprehensive supplications and would leave aside lengthy supplications other than these."""
"4950","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to set out on a journey on Thursday."""
"4951","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Sweet water would be brought for him (peace and blessings be upon him) from the houses of as-Suqya; in one narration: sweet water would be fetched for him from the well of as-Suqya."""
"4952","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would seek forgiveness for the front row three times and for the second row once."""
"4953","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wipe semen off his garment with a stalk of idhkhir grass and then pray in it, and when it was dry he would scrape it off and then pray in it."""
"4954","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would call a mare (a female horse) 'faras'."""
"4955","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""It distressed him (peace and blessings be upon him) that any unpleasant odour should be perceived from him."""
"4956","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would drink water in three breaths, saying Bismillah at the beginning and Alhamdulillah at the end."""
"4957","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would make a gesture during the prayer (when the need arose)."""
"4958","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would tilt the vessel for a cat so that it could drink from it, and then he would perform ablution with the water it had left."""
"4959","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray the forenoon (Duha) prayer as four rak'ahs, and would add to it as much as Allah willed."""
"4960","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray the forenoon (Duha) prayer as six rak'ahs."""
"4961","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray at night two rak'ahs at a time, then after concluding with salam he would use the tooth-stick (miswak)."""
"4962","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would offer voluntary prayer between Maghrib and Isha."""
"4963","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray on a small mat."""
"4964","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray on a spread (rug)."""
"4965","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would offer voluntary prayer on his mount, whichever direction it faced, but when he intended to offer an obligatory prayer, he would dismount and face the Qiblah."""
"4966","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray in his sandals."""
"4967","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the sun had passed its zenith, He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray four rak'ahs before Zuhr, and he would say: 'When the sun passes its zenith, the gates of the heaven are opened.'"""
"4968","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after Maghrib in his house, and two rak'ahs after Isha; and he would not pray after Jumu'ah until he had gone back, then he would pray two rak'ahs in his house."""
"4969","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray thirteen rak'ahs at night, including the Witr and the two Sunnah rak'ahs of Fajr."""
"4970","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would fast on Monday and Thursday."""
"4971","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would fast on Saturday, Sunday and Monday in one month, and on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday in the next month."""
"4972","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would fast three days from the beginning of every month, and it was rare that he would not be fasting on Friday."""
"4973","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sacrifice two horned, black-and-white rams, and he would say Bismillah and the takbir."""
"4974","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would punish the one who drank wine with sandals and palm branches."""
"4975","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would place his right hand over his left hand in the prayer."""
"4976","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would have horses specially trained for racing."""
"4977","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would go to all of his wives in a single night with a single ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"4978","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""It pleased him (peace and blessings be upon him), when he went out for some task, to hear the words: 'O Rashid (rightly guided one)! O Najih (successful one)!'"""
"4979","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked the thick residue at the bottom of the cooking pot."""
"4980","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked what was cold and sweet."""
"4981","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked the foreleg of the goat."""
"4982","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked a good dream."""
"4983","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked a pleasant fragrance."""
"4984","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to hold a dry date-palm stalk in his hand."""
"4985","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked good omens and disliked taking evil omens."""
"4986","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked gourd."""
"4987","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to meet the enemy in battle at the time when the sun had passed its zenith."""
"4988","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When He (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived, he would be recognised by his fragrance."""
"4989","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would count his tasbih on his fingers."""
"4990","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would repeat an important statement three times so that it would be understood."""
"4991","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ritual bath (ghusl) with one sa' of water and perform ablution with one mudd of water."""
"4992","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) and one of his wives would both perform the ritual bath (ghusl) from a single vessel."""
"4993","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wash his seat three times."""
"4994","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would change an unpleasant name."""
"4995","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would break his fast with fresh dates before praying; if there were no fresh dates, then with dried dates; and if there were no dried dates either, he would take a few sips of water."""
"4996","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would himself pick the lice from his garment, milk his own goat, and do his own work."""
"4997","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss some of his wives, then pray without performing ablution."""
"4998","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss his wife while fasting."""
"4999","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would accept a gift and give something in return for it."""
"5000","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite verse by verse: 'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of the worlds,' then pause; then 'The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' then pause."""
"5001","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When reproaching someone, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: 'What is the matter with him? May his forehead be covered in dust!'"""
"5002","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would get up when he heard the crowing rooster."""
"5003","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would stand in prayer at night for so long that his blessed feet would crack."""
"5004","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""On the day of Eid al-Fitr, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would keep saying the takbir from the time he left his house until he reached the Eid prayer ground."""
"5005","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would remember Allah abundantly, speak little idle talk, make the prayer long and the sermon short, and he felt no disdain, nor was he too proud, to walk with a widow, a poor person or a slave until he had fulfilled his need."""
"5006","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked 'shikal' (a particular kind of marking) in a horse."""
"5007","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked unnecessary questions and found fault with them, but when Abu Razin asked him, he would answer him, and he was pleased with what he said."""
"5008","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked that food be taken from the top (middle) of the dish."""
"5009","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked that anyone should tread on his heels; rather, they should walk to the right or the left."""
"5010","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would wear sandals of tanned leather and dye his beard yellow with wars and saffron."""
"5011","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would glance to the right and left in prayer, but he would not turn his neck to look behind him."""
"5012","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would press his chest and face against the Multazam."""
"5013","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would draw out his voice at length when reciting the Qur'an."""
"5014","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by children, he would greet them with salam."""
"5015","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When he (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by women, he would greet them with salam."""
"5016","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) walked in such a manner that it was clear he was neither weak nor lazy."""
"5017","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sleep in the first part of the night and bring the last part to life with worship."""
"5018","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sleep until he began to snore, then get up and pray without performing a new ablution."""
"5019","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would sometimes sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) without even touching water."""
"5020","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would slaughter his sacrificial animal at the Eid prayer ground."""
"5021","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""After concluding the prayer with salam, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would turn away towards his right."""
"5022","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When reciting ruqyah, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would blow lightly."""
"5023","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray witr while riding a camel."""
"5024","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray witr at the beginning, the middle and the end of the night, in every part of it."""
"5025","It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He (peace and blessings be upon him) would play with Zaynab bint Umm Salamah and say again and again: 'O Zuwaynib! O Zuwaynib!'"""
